      {
        "review_id": 714381280,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r714381280-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Confronting ",
        "text": "I visited the area as part of a group tour with a Nepali guide. We were advised to keep an eye on our belongings and stay with the group. Being foreigners, we weren’t allowed to access the temple, but we walked along the river. There are ‘holy men’ dressed in orange who are keen to be photographed for a fee and a few market stalls. Our Hindu guide was excited to have us watch a Hindu cremation. It was quite confronting to watch the deceased person’s body being washed by family members and moved to the cremation alter. It was at this point that my daughter and I walked away from the group as we didn’t wish to see the body alight. Sitting a short distance from the group, we were approached by a man who offered to purchase my teenage daughter from me. Thankfully our group arrived at this point and our guide shooed him away. Quite confronting. ",
        "review_tip": null,
