        "title": "Hindu/Buddhist shrine",
        "text": "We visited the day after the festival of Deej when ladies in their finest costumes queue for hours to pray for spiritual enlightenment. This is a big date in their calendar and is a wonderful spectacle to see the ladies in their finery. The temple complex has some areas off limits to those not of the Hindu/Buddhist faith but the architecture is tremendous and there are a number of private gatherings having services provided which can be observed and enjoyed by visitors which gives a good insight into these religions. Next to the temple complex is the river where cremations can be observed.",
